# Task 0 – ROS Installation

This task involved installing and configuring the Robot Operating System (ROS) environment for robotics development.

## Steps Performed

1. Installed Ubuntu (recommended OS for ROS)
2. Installed ROS distribution
3. Configured ROS environment variables
4. Created a ROS workspace
5. Tested ROS installation using basic commands

## Commands Used

sudo apt update
sudo apt install ros-humble-desktop

source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash

## Outcome

Successfully configured the ROS development environment required for future robotics tasks.
